# Continent layout map — terrain preview (future)

A mistaken interpretation once implemented (then removed) a **top-down heightmap preview on the 2D Continent Layout Map**. The user clarified they wanted **neighbor regions in the 3D editor** for seam moulding instead — but they explicitly want this 2D idea kept for later:

> It would make for a very good map further down the road.

## Intended future feature

When building a richer continent / world map UI:

- Optional toggle: show **baked top-down terrain thumbnails** on each region tile (not live WebGL).
- Efficient path (already prototyped once):
  - Downsample heights to ~64² (shared helper like `downsampleRegionHeights` / `REGION_LAYOUT_PREVIEW_SIZE`).
  - Lightweight API e.g. `GET /api/regions/:id/layout-preview` returning heights + colorGrading (not full blueprint).
  - CPU canvas bake (elevation + fake slope shade from groundTint/biome); cache per region id.
  - Open region can bake from live `RegionEditorScene` heights (unsaved sculpt).
- Keep it **opt-in** so the layout map stays cheap when editing origins only.

## Do not confuse with

**World → Show neighbor regions** in the 3D editor = read-only adjacent terrain for moulding seams. That is the current seam-authoring tool; the 2D height preview is a separate map UX enhancement.
